UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Queen of Pentacles represents the absolute archetype of ''Systemic Integration and Ecosystemic Abundance''—the mature, receptive phase where the sovereign consciousness seamlessly integrates material resource management with profound emotional stability and natural alignment. Moving beyond the relentless execution of the Knight, the Queen signifies the stage of ''The Sovereign Matriarch,'' where you purposefully establish an environment that is not just productive, but deeply nurturing, generative, and secure. Visually depicted as a regal figure seated on a throne carved with symbols of nature, surrounded by a lush, thriving landscape while holding a single pentacle with tender, protective awareness, this archetype embodies the concept of ''Sovereign Stewardship''—the realization that true material mastery is the capacity to foster sustainable growth, warmth, and security for oneself and the wider ecosystem. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of ''Resource Harmonization,'' where you are running stabilized, high-efficiency processes that balance outer productivity with inner well-being, ensuring that your physical foundations support your spiritual and creative life. When the Queen of Pentacles appears, your system is registering an ''Ecosystemic Health'' status; you are being invited to stop the anxious hustle and instead lean into the grounded, practical power of your established abundance. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your self-care and baseline security. You are being tasked with the essential work of ''Intentional Nurturing'': ensuring that your physical body, your home, and your personal domain are managed with love, practicality, and absolute technical grace, making your space a sanctuary of sustainable power.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Queen of Pentacles appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of ''Systemic Disruption, Domestic Inertia,'' or the catastrophic mutation of healthy stewardship into smothering control, material insecurity, or superficial attachment to comfort—a state where you are effectively ''leaking your personal energy into keeping up appearances'' while your internal foundations are in a state of neglect. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates ''possessive micro-management or material hoarding'' with ''maintaining security,'' even as your actual, internal operating system is experiencing a critical failure of its genuine self-sustenance protocols. You are essentially ''suffocating your own growth,'' running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to ''control the environment'' over the sober, unglamorous requirement to nurture your own inner space. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the ''grounded, capable provider,'' while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of financial anxiety, physical neglect, or codependency, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency resentment, the experience of ''smothering those around you with material control,'' and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your comfort is a fragile shield against inner chaos. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a ''feedback loop of superficial security and emotional codependency''; you are obsessively trying to fix outer details, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final peace is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to stop managing everyone else, you would have to face the raw reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these anxious, controlling, comfort-obsessed scripts, perform a brutal audit of your self-care practices, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize genuine, internal well-being over the convenience of a polished external facade. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance dependency, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority.'
WHERE id = 55;
